<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plumbāgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			f.
		plumbum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A species of lead ore</i>, <i>black-lead</i>, <i>plumbago</i>, <i>also called</i> molybdaena, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				18, 50, § 168</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a leaden color</i>
			in gems, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 5, 18, §
			68</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>also called</i>
			molybdaena, <i>leadwort</i>, <i>fleawort</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 13, 97, §
		155</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
